I wasn't looking to make any built  guides in your time soon because there  are thousands of them out there all  working towards the absolute min max  detail for any situation but I've been  talking to a number of people that are  struggling in the early stages of the  raid both of my squad and on other  platforms they have no idea where to  start so I've been putting together a  simple cheat sheet of sorts to help  people with what they need to prepare  for the raid I wasn't intending to make  a video for it however it does make it a  little bit easy to explain this way in  the super quick video I hope to give  first-time Raiders who are struggling to  get past the first boss on this raid and  easy to understand starting point for  the build q intro  [Music]  okay enough of that  let's crack into it this raid is all  about DPS builds and this is true all  the way through but for the purpose of  this video we're just gonna focus on the  first boss boomer on the screen right  now is a summary of what I'll be talking  about for the remainder of the video so  if you weren't wondering why I picked  these talents etc you could probably  just take a screenshot and leave  otherwise I'll carry on when it first  stepped into the raid I thought my  tried-and-true PvE build that was able  to carry me through any old heroic  content Solo would be more than capable  truth be told it was reasonably DPS  heavy so if everyone is running  something similar we may have been okay  but this wasn't the case most of us up  until now have been able to run through  the most difficult content in the game  without worrying too much about their  builds to most people's surprise and in  some cases disgust they made this raid  very difficult requiring team  coordination first and built scope with  it as a close second I love this it's  completely changed the way I feel about  the division to the need to focus more  on builds was well over jus I do hope  they introduce the need for a larger  variety of builds and later rates but  that's more of a discussion for later on  as I said before you need war damage  that's it  you could add a little bit of armor and  health to if you'd like but because of  the difficulty of the enemies and the  time limit behind killing the boss you  need to act fast I'm not going to go  into the boss mechanics too much there  are plenty of videos out there on how to  do it but to sum it up the boss can only  be dropped to his knees by taking out  his bag using a turret you'll think of  in a very small window to deal as much  damage as possible to him you have to  continue with ads you have to contend  with this healing chess piece and you  only have about ten minutes to kill him  before he destroys the two turrets team  coordination is important or you would  never be able to drop them with time and  repetition this can be learnt but a few  as a team aren't doing enough damage  you'll never be taken down in time I'm  gonna keep repeating myself in hopes  that it sticks damage is king in this  raid this is more important than any  other build attribute to make this  easier to follow I'll be using a build  that are quickly threw together in a  couple of hours using only the minimal  gear a head-on ant and a quick farming  run this build is far from optimized the  weapon I'm using doesn't even have  active talent unlocked but the point I'm  trying to make is around the type of  pieces you should be looking out for to  be fair this build is actually more than  what you need to play your part in the  raid there are just a lot of pieces that  we could be further tweaked like a hell  of a lot more health and even more  damage you'll notice straight away this  is very damaged heavy and my attention  to armor and health is quite minimal the  first time around the raid I was  actually using a build with ok damage  and around 300k armor after changing  towards a more glass cannon type build  with no sustain I was worried oh it's  gonna be a little bit too squishy but I  can honestly say I haven't noticed the  difference the enemies had so hard that  my high armor and health were pretty  much being ignored before I get into it  this has been built for PC but i'll be  making suggestions for console as a go  along you should be focusing on the  following when looking at your build  first weapon damage this is a priority  over everything else second damage to  elites if you can get this over 50%  you're doing pretty well  and lastly headshot damage or critical  hit damage and chance if you're on  console here chop damage is actually  less important as you go through the  raid as you'll be facing things that  won't have a hit to shoot like the war  dogs so for this reason focus on weapon  damage and damage to elites first mask  hard-hitting damage to elites there  really isn't another mask talent better  than this one for the raid make sure you  also get the damage to elites attribute  on this piece too as you can get a  fairly high percentage body armor  berserk plus ten percent within damage  for missing 20% of armor depleted I  would usually prefer to run unstoppable  force on this piece but it can be  difficult to activate this talent when  you need it especially if you're in the  role more focused on the turret and the  boss given how hard the enemies hit  you'll often find yourself in low armor  which is where this talent really shines  for this reason I like to run minimal  armor and high health usually you'll  find me running around with no armor at  all gaining another 50% weapon don't  depending on the piece you find you  could also run a second talent with  hard-hitting for more damage to elites  or vital for plus 20% health holster  hard-hitting damage to elites or weapon  damage or precise which is hit shot  damaged or if you're struggling or on  console either critical hit chance or  damage  backpack hard-hitting and on the ropes  for an extra 25 percent weapon damage of  went both of your skills are uncool down  I usually hate this talent because I'm  not a big fan of being forced into using  skills especially if they're there to  keep you alive when needed but in this  situation it's worth it but vital for an  extra 20% health could also be useful  gloves again hard-hitting damage to  elites or weapon damage seeing a trend  here however if you've built up a  certain amount of critical hit chance  clutch could really help you out with a  boost to your health for each critical  hit kneepads for solar PV play  I love patients it's a subtle armor heal  will taking cover but in the raid you  don't often get the chance to stay still  for very long especially in the Boomer  buff stage plus because we want our  armor to actually stay low for berserk  it's good to get rid of this plus any  other armor on kill mods and stared  focus on the same old hard-hitting  damage to elites brand sets if you get  to the point of being able to focus on a  brand set and go down the moon maxing  path continue to look for things that  will assist you with your damage with  anti damage heat shock damage critical  hit damage etc weapons because of the  short period of time you get to dull  damage on boomer and how hard the NPC's  hit focus on burst damage  I prefer assault rifles hard fast damage  with a decent amount of range on console  you may find it easier with the SMG  you'll need to give a little closer but  you'll have the added advantage of  having the built-in critical hit chance  as far as weapon mods and talents follow  the same trend as the riskier build more  damage if I was playing on console I  would ignore the headshot damage and  focus fully on credit damage and chance  but regardless of platform weapon damage  and damage to elites is the first  priority you are very squishy with this  build but given what you're coming up  against a little bit of extra armor  isn't going to help you use cover but  don't sittin up for too long you'll  likely either be flanked or unable to  help the team when taking on the boss  keep moving and bursting any MPC's you  come across although you can't take too  many hits you'll usually be firing at  enemies who are focusing on someone else  there is neat man team use the numbers  to your advantage last but not least  please dear God  when the turret runner calls that boomer  is down  what you're doing and shoot the boss  coming up against boomer you want to be  doing at least 50k damage per assault  rifle bullet but even with this crudely  thrown-together build I've shown above  you should be heading them for a minimum  of ATK per bullet which is more than  enough if you're still struggling with  these numbers it's your team  coordination that's leading you down  this video was really just intended for  some of the crew in the ng and discord  not knowing where to start but there  might be a few others that find this  useful - apologies this video certainly  hasn't followed the same sort of  production quality that I try to achieve  with most but there was a bit of an  urgent need for this one before people  start jumping into the next run of raid  attempts plus I didn't have any raid  footage to go along with it because I  forgot to click the damn record button  hopefully this has been found somewhat  useful for some of you as I said there's  a huge number of options available this  is just one part you could take anyway  let me know if you have any questions  and good luck taking down that big burly  beast Cheers  [Music]  you
 

